    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="0744" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/9–444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Appointed Minister to Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-04T08:00:00+03:06">September 4,
                            1944—8 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>264. Jordan told me today: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Highly qualified Indian Muslim already selected and available for
                            financial adviser to King whenever our two Governments agree.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>British Military Mission at Taif being reinforced by mobile repair
                            units and 22 personnel.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Eastern Bank has requested Saudi Government for permission to open
                            branch in Saudi Arabia on Persian Gulf, obviously a move to match
                            National City Bank.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d799-f1"/>
                        </item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>He rejects proposal to explain budget to Saudi officials. (See
                            Department’s 166, August 23, 9 p.m.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d799-f2"
                            />)</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>He proposes MESC plan to supervise food reserves in controlled
                            warehouses.</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>He declines to leave statement of present food reserves and overall
                            needs to MESC Jidda, claiming they lack experience and facts.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0745" n="733" xml:id="pg733"/>
                <p>MESC conference in Jidda this week will be crucial in determining Jordan’s
                    ability to dominate MESC British personnel and in arriving at satisfactory
                    supply program.</p>
                <p>Details by pouch.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d799-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eddy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d799-f1" n="44" xml:id="d799-f1-content">
                <p>The National City Bank of New York had requested permission from the Saudi
                    Arabian Government to open a branch at Ras Tanura.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d799-f2" n="43" xml:id="d799-f2-content">
